g, etc. So I built a little language server and a vscode extension which adds syntax highlighting. Note-taking now feels more like writing code, and I get to use my favorite vscode keybindings (vim). Feedback is welcome!\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"I've been writing notes as plain text files since forever, and it occurred to me that note-taking could benefit from the typical features that a language server provides: clickable links, autocomplete, hover previews, formatting, diagnostics, refactoring, etc. So I built a little language server and a vscode extension which adds syntax highlighting. Note-taking now feels more like writing code, and I get to use my favorite vscode keybindings (vim). Feedback is welcome!","submitter_user":"lettuce","user_is_author":true,"tags":["editors"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/xcacrh","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/xcacrh/mull_note_taking_with_language_server"},{"short_id":"gtev9y","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:39:23.630-05:00","title":"Lessons learned building Fronteira, an MCP proxy with behavioral guardrails","url":"https://wiki.alcidesfonseca.com/blog/lessons-learned-building-fronteira/","score":-2,"flags":3,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"alcides","user_is_author":true,"tags":["security","vibecoding"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/gtev9y","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/gtev9y/lessons_learned_building_fronteira_mcp"},{"short_id":"6laoto","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:02:05.882-05:00","title":"The road to iroh 1.0","url":"https://www.iroh.computer/blog/the-road-to-iroh-1-0","score":30,"flags":1,"comment_count":6,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"Frando","user_is_author":false,"tags":["networking"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/6laoto","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/6laoto/road_iroh_1_0"},{"short_id":"vvtzdj","created_at":"2026-10-16T06:26:57.346-05:00","title":"What agents mean for Rust (and vice versa)","url":"https://small